uestion" "q-123005" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-8)=3{t}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{4}+5t)=4{t}^{3}+5\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{3}\\sqrt{{(3{t}^{2})}^{2}+{(4{t}^{3}+5)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{3}\\sqrt{9{t}^{4}+16{t}^{6}+40{t}^{3}+25}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{3}\\sqrt{16{t}^{6}+9{t}^{4}+40{t}^{3}+25}\\,\\text{d}t\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "880b4c305cb48e839fe011b7427b25ba4982ca8d1307913ab8cbf1afbc395e00"} {"question" "q-123005" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "76f1416cb6770f11d9b437e963585d4132b9f73be015e972b94b9a278e54e487"} {"question" "q-123005" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "880b4c305cb48e839fe011b7427b25ba4982ca8d1307913ab8cbf1afbc395e00"} {"question" "q-123005" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2{\\int }_{-2}^{3}\\sqrt{8{t}^{6}+9{t}^{4}+20{t}^{3}+25}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "3{\\int }_{-2}^{3}\\sqrt{{t}^{6}+{t}^{4}+{t}^{3}+25}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-2}^{3}\\sqrt{16{t}^{6}+49{t}^{4}+25}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-2}^{3}\\sqrt{16{t}^{6}+9{t}^{4}+40{t}^{3}+25}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-2}^{3}\\sqrt{4{t}^{6}+3{t}^{4}+4{t}^{3}+5}\\,\\text{d}t"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "880b4c305cb48e839fe011b7427b25ba4982ca8d1307913ab8cbf1afbc395e00"} {"question" "q-123005" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{-2}^{3}\\sqrt{16{t}^{6}+9{t}^{4}+40{t}^{3}+25}\\,\\text{d}t"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "880b4c305cb48e839fe011b7427b25ba4982ca8d1307913ab8cbf1afbc395e00"} {"question" "q-21354" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following gives the length of the curve defined by the parametric equations\n$x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t),\\,y=t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)$\nfrom $t=0$ to $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ ?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "880b4c305cb48e839fe011b7427b25ba4982ca8d1307913ab8cbf1afbc395e00"} {"question" "q-21354" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t))=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t))=1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t))^{2}+(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t))^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡(t)+{sin}^{2}⁡(t)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)+1+{cos}^{2}⁡(t)-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+1+{cos}^{2}⁡(t)-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{2+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)+{cos}^{2}⁡(t)}\\,\\text{d}t\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "880b4c305cb48e839fe011b7427b25ba4982ca8d1307913ab8cbf1afbc395e00"} {"question" "q-21354" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "76f1416cb6770f11d9b437e963585d4132b9f73be015e972b94b9a278e54e487"} {"question" "q-21354" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "880b4c305cb48e839fe011b7427b25ba4982ca8d1307913ab8cbf1afbc395e00"} {"question" "q-21354" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answ