{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{5}\\sqrt{(1+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t))^{2}+(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t))^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{5}\\sqrt{1+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)+4{cos}^{2}⁡(t)+4{sin}^{2}⁡(2t)}\\,\\text{d}t\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "880b4c305cb48e839fe011b7427b25ba4982ca8d1307913ab8cbf1afbc395e00"} {"question" "q-15163" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "76f1416cb6770f11d9b437e963585d4132b9f73be015e972b94b9a278e54e487"} {"question" "q-15163" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "880b4c305cb48e839fe011b7427b25ba4982ca8d1307913ab8cbf1afbc395e00"} {"question" "q-15163" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{2}^{5}\\sqrt{1+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)+16{cos}^{2}⁡(t)+4{sin}^{2}⁡(2t)}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{2}^{5}\\sqrt{1+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)+2{cos}^{2}⁡(t)+4{sin}^{2}⁡(2t)}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{2}^{5}\\sqrt{1+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)+4{cos}^{2}⁡(t)+16{sin}^{2}⁡(2t)}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{2}^{5}\\sqrt{1+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)+4{cos}^{2}⁡(t)+4{sin}^{2}⁡(2t)}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{2}^{5}\\sqrt{1+8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)+16{cos}^{2}⁡(t)+16{sin}^{2}⁡(2t)}\\,\\text{d}t"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "880b4c305cb48e839fe011b7427b25ba4982ca8d1307913ab8cbf1afbc395e00"} {"question" "q-15163" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{2}^{5}\\sqrt{1+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)+4{cos}^{2}⁡(t)+4{sin}^{2}⁡(2t)}\\,\\text{d}t"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "880b4c305cb48e839fe011b7427b25ba4982ca8d1307913ab8cbf1afbc395e00"} {"question" "q-10256" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/assets/da529910e268ea4c124d7c27b085ca1799e255604459c539cc8d5809dda8f95a.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx={sin}^{3}⁡t,\\,y={cos}^{3}⁡t,\\,t\\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "880b4c305cb48e839fe011b7427b25ba4982ca8d1307913ab8cbf1afbc395e00"} {"question" "q-10256" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({sin}^{3}⁡t)=3{sin}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({cos}^{3}⁡t)=-3{cos}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{(3{sin}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)}^{2}+{(-3{cos}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{9{sin}^{4}⁡t{cos}^{2}⁡t+9{cos}^{4}⁡t{sin}^{2}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{9{sin}^{2}⁡t{cos}^{2}⁡t({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t){|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi -\\operatorname{cos}⁡0) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}(-1-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "880b4c305cb48e839fe011b7427b25ba4982ca8d1307913ab8cbf1afbc395e00"} {"question" "q-10256" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "76f1416cb6770f11d9b437e963585d4132b9f73be015e972b94b9a278e54e487"} {"question" "q-10256" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "880b4c305cb48e839fe011b7427b25ba4982ca8d1307913ab8cbf1afbc395e00"} {"question" "q-10256" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "880b4c305cb48e839fe011b7427b25ba4982ca8d1307913ab8cbf1afbc395e00"} {"question" "q-10256" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "880b4c305cb48e839fe011b7427b25ba4982ca8d1307913ab8cbf1afbc395e00"} {"question" "q-351505" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/assets/893efa56ec41ef2242a48831ad4f58b23edc791464ccc7dcb4dd104b87843360.png)\n\nFind the arc length $L$ of the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=t-\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3},\\,y={t}^{2},\\,t\\in [0,3].\n$$\n\nDo not round the answer.\n\n$L=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "880b4c305cb48e839fe011b7427b25ba4982ca8d1307913ab8cbf1afbc395e00"} {"question" "q-351505" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t-\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}) \\\\  & =1-{t}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}) \\\\  & =2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\sqrt{(1-{t}^{2})^{2}+(2t)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\sqrt{1-2{t}^{2}+{t}^{4}+4{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\sqrt{1+2{t}^{2}+{t}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\sqrt{(1+{t}^{2})^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(1+{t}^{2})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(t+\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3})\\,{|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =(3+\\frac{27}{3})-0 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "880b4c305cb48e839fe011b7427b25ba4982ca8d1307913ab8cbf1afbc395e00"} {"question" "q-351505" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "76f1416cb6770f11d9b437e963585d4132b9f73be015e972b94b9a278e54e487"} {"question" "q-351505" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "880b4c305cb48e839fe011b7427b25ba4982ca8d1307913ab8cbf1afbc395e00"} {"question" "q-351505" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "12"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "880b4c305cb48e839fe011b7427b25ba4982ca8d1307913ab8cbf1afbc395e00"} {"question" "q-351439" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/assets/0b9c4ebc430e05ef205e3d8108f2e1649bbc51b1a6b54e8f47b48e7ddad1e9a6.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve $L$ defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=4{cos}^{3}⁡t,\\,y=4{sin}^{3}⁡t,\\,t\\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{4}].\n$$\n\nDo not round the answer.\n\n$L=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "880b4c305cb48e839fe011b7427b25ba4982ca8d1307913ab8cbf1afbc395e00"} {"question" "q-351439" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{cos}^{3}⁡t) \\\\  & =4\\cdot 3{cos}^{2}⁡t\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\  & =-12\\operatorname{sin}⁡t{cos}^{2}⁡t,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{sin}^{3}⁡t) \\\\  & =4\\cdot 3{sin}^{2}⁡t\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\  & =12{sin}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{{(-12\\operatorname{sin}⁡t{cos}^{2}⁡t)}^{2}+{(12{sin}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{144{sin}^{2}⁡t{cos}^{4}⁡t+144{sin}^{4}⁡t{cos}^{2}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{144{sin}^{2}⁡t{cos}^{2}⁡t({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{144{sin}^{2}⁡t{cos}^{2}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}12|\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t|\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}12\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =6{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡0 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "880b4c305cb48e839fe011b7427b25ba4982ca8d1307913ab8cbf1afbc395e00"} {"question" "q-351439" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "76f1416cb6770f11d9b437e963585d4132b9f73be015e972b94b9a278e54e487"} {"question" "q-351439" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "880b4c305cb48e839fe011b7427b25ba4982ca8d1307913ab8cbf1afbc395e00"} {"question" "q-351439" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "880b4c305cb48e839fe011b7427b25ba4982ca8d1307913ab8cbf1afbc395e00"} {"question" "q-351474" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/assets/cf06561072376949c6df49aec94b45c57b1cd43fbb031ea7b157ea5dfbac877a.png)\n\nFind the arc length $L$ of the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{9}(6t+1)^{3/2},\\,y=\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{2},\\,t\\in [0,1].\n$$\n\nDo not round the answer.\n\n$L=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "880b4c305cb48e839fe011b7427b25ba4982ca8d1307913ab8cbf1afbc395e00"} {"question" "q-351474" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{9}(6t+1)^{3/2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}(6t+1)^{1/2}\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =(6t+1)^{1/2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =3t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{{((6t+1)^{1/2})}^{2}+(3t)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{6t+1+9{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{(3t+1)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}|3t+1|\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(3t+1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(\\frac{3{t}^{2}}{2}+t)\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{3}{2}+1)-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "880b4c305cb48e839fe011b7427b25ba4982ca8d1307913ab8cbf1afbc395e00"} {"question" "q-351474" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "76f1416cb6770f11d9b437e963585d4132b9f73be015e972b94b9a278e54e487"} {"question" "q-351474" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "880b4c305cb48e839fe011b7427b25ba4982ca8d1307913ab8cbf1afbc395e00"} {"question" "q-351474" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "880b4c305cb48e839fe011b7427b25ba4982ca8d1307913ab8cbf1afbc395e00"} {"question" "q-10255" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/assets/ac040bc2c3eb943f947f34602c7c03e90f18e129a0fa7749d8ae60faaab12f71.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,y=1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,t\\in [0,\\pi ].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "880b4c305cb48e839fe011b7427b25ba4982ca8d1307913ab8cbf1afbc395e00"} {"question" "q-10255" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)=1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{{(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)}^{2}+{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{2-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to the double-angle formula for cosine, $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )=1-2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .$ Substituting $\\theta =\\frac{t}{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{t}{2}) & =1-2{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{t}{2}) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t & =1-2{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{t}{2}) \\\\ 1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & =2{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{t}{2}) \\\\ 2-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & =4{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{t}{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{2-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{4{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{t}{2})}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{t}{2})\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-2\\cdot 2\\cdot {\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{t}{2})|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =-4(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡0) \\\\  & =-4(0-1) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "880b4c305cb48e839fe011b7427b25ba4982ca8d1307913ab8cbf1afbc395e00"} {"question" "q-10255" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "76f1416cb6770f11d9b437e963585d4132b9f73be015e972b94b9a278e54e487"} {"question" "q-10255" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "880b4c305cb48e839fe011b7427b25ba4982ca8d1307913ab8cbf1afbc395e00"} {"question" "q-10255" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\pi "] ["math" "4"] ["math" "4\\pi "] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "\\pi "]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "880b4c305cb48e839fe011b7427b25ba4982ca8d1307913ab8cbf1afbc395e00"} {"question" "q-10255" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "880b4c305cb48e839fe011b7427b25ba4982ca8d1307913ab8cbf1afbc395e00"} {"question" "e-602" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/assets/834eff403ac2a6f696e104ec914cac1b951f8a6d989e11c0e9f2576ac9e7f0d8.png)\n\nFind an integral expression for the arc length of the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=1-t, \\quad y= \\dfrac{2}{3} t^{3/2}, \\qquad t\\in[0,1].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/example-602.json" "file_sha256" "1f357f0ff72d7e19f94ea030095cc693c81863dbdaa0c179e931b9bd339205f9"} {"question" "e-602" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL = \\int_{t_1}^{t_2} \\sqrt{ \\left( \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}x}{\\textrm{d}t}\\right)^2 + \\left( \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}t}\\right)^2}\\:\\textrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-t)=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{2}{3}{t}^{3/2})={t}^{1/2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{{(-1)}^{2}+{({t}^{1/2})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{1+t}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/example-602.json" "file_sha256" "1f357f0ff72d7e19f94ea030095cc693c81863dbdaa0c179e931b9bd339205f9"} {"question" "e-7130" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the expression that gives the length of the curve defined by the parametric equations\n$x=t, \\, y=\\ln{(\\cos{t})}$\nfrom $t=0$ to $t=\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}$ (see graph below).\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/assets/48de26c11ae08afb45ec19ee56e770f7418f9be2afb8ee7dd46a0d1136cb125b.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/example-7130.json" "file_sha256" "4b95462ac1beffe8f0371d72dcd570adcc4453d9a18adb64c59c806e57e25794"} {"question" "e-7130" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL = \\int_{t_1}^{t_2} \\sqrt{ \\left( \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}x}{\\textrm{d}t}\\right)^2 + \\left( \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}t}\\right)^2}\\:\\textrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t))=-\\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{{(1)}^{2}+{(-\\operatorname{tan}⁡t)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{1+{tan}^{2}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{{sec}^{2}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/example-7130.json" "file_sha256" "4b95462ac1beffe8f0371d72dcd570adcc4453d9a18adb64c59c806e57e25794"} {"question" "e-603" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the arc length of the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=e^t(\\cos{t}+\\sin{t}), \\quad y=e^t(\\cos{t}-\\sin{t}) , \\quad t\\in \\left[0,\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}\\right].\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/assets/15d185178bf8882f837c19361d630c0e537e145ca2337cad4655677255d0348a.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/example-603.json" "file_sha256" "0b1465a151789c1895ad8501865c5beb11207ea792c1f50fd326b697b35d37a8"} {"question" "e-603" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Computing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)) \\\\  & ={e}^{t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+{e}^{t}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t) \\\\  & =2{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)) \\\\  & ={e}^{t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+{e}^{t}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t) \\\\  & =-2{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{{(2{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)}^{2}+{(-2{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{4{e}^{2t}({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}2{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2{e}^{t}{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =2({e}^{\\pi /4}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/example-603.json" "file_sha256" "0b1465a151789c1895ad8501865c5beb11207ea792c1f50fd326b697b35d37a8"}] "usage" {"e-7130" [] "e-603" [] "e-602" [] "q-10255" []} "basis" 1148 "retractions" [[17592186092418 :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/997/Source/Images/q-10255.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve defined parametrically as\n$x = t - \\sin t, y = 1 - \\cos t, t \\in  [0, \\pi ]$."] [17592186092028 :question/problem "Find an integral expression for the arc length of the curve defined parametrically as\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/997/Source/Images/c85ca457e7f02850924980f54ba585bf.png)\n\n$x=1-t, \\quad y= \\dfrac{2}{3} t^{3/2}, \\qquad t\\in[0,1]$."] [17592186092028 :question/worked-solution "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL = \\int_{t_1}^{t_2} \\sqrt{\\left(\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}x}{\\textrm{d}t}\\right)^2 + \\left(\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}t}\\right)^2}\\:\\textrm{d}t\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dx}{dt} &= \\frac{d}{dt}(1 - t) =-1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dy}{dt} &= \\frac{d}{dt}(\\frac{2}{3}t^{3/2}) = t^{1/2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL &= \\int _{t_{1}}^{t_{2}}\\sqrt{(\\frac{dx}{dt})^{2} + (\\frac{dy}{dt})^{2}}dt \\\\\n&= \\int _{0}^{1}\\sqrt{(-1)^{2} + (t^{1/2})^{2}}dt \\\\\n&= \\int _{0}^{1}\\sqrt{1 + t}dt\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186092060 :question/problem "Find the expression that gives the length of the curve defined by the parametric equations\n$x=t, \\, y=\\ln{(\\cos{t})}$\nfrom $t=0$ to $t=\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}$ (see graph below).\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/997/Source/Images/f10352be16212d467425c8695c797467.png)"] [17592186092060 :question/worked-solution "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL = \\int_{t_1}^{t_2} \\sqrt{\\left(\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}x}{\\textrm{d}t}\\right)^2 + \\left(\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}t}\\right)^2}\\:\\textrm{d}t\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dx}{dt} &= \\frac{d}{dt}(t) = 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dy}{dt} &= \\frac{d}{dt}(\\ln (\\cos t)) =-\\tan t\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL &= \\int _{t_{1}}^{t_{2}}\\sqrt{(\\frac{dx}{dt})^{2} + (\\frac{dy}{dt})^{2}}dt \\\\\n&= \\int _{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{(1)^{2} + (-\\tan t)^{2}}dt \\\\\n&= \\int _{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{1 + \\tan^{2} t}dt \\\\\n&= \\int _{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{\\sec^{2} t}dt \\\\\n&= \\int _{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sec tdt\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186092029 :question/problem "Find the arc length of the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$x=e^t(\\cos{t}+\\sin{t}), \\quad y=e^t(\\cos{t}-\\sin{t}), \\quad t\\in \\left[0,\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}\\right]$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/997/Source/Images/01cb59beb0b1df4a0cf0402429bafa19.png)"] [17592186092029 :question/worked-solution "Computing the derivatives of $x$ and $y$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dx}{dt} &= \\frac{d}{dt}(e^{t}(\\cos t + \\sin t)) \\\\\n&= e^{t}(\\cos t + \\sin t) + e^{t}(-\\sin t + \\cos t) \\\\\n&= 2e^{t}\\cos t\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dy}{dt} &= \\frac{d}{dt}(e^{t}(\\cos t - \\sin t)) \\\\\n&= e^{t}(\\cos t - \\sin t) + e^{t}(-\\sin t - \\cos t) \\\\\n&=-2e^{t}\\sin t\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL &= \\int _{t_{1}}^{t_{2}}\\sqrt{(\\frac{dx}{dt})^{2} + (\\frac{dy}{dt})^{2}}dt \\\\\n&= \\int _{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{(2e^{t}\\cos t)^{2} + (-2e^{t}\\sin t)^{2}}dt \\\\\n&= \\int _{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{4e^{2t}(\\cos^{2} t + \\sin^{2} t)}dt \\\\\n&= \\int _{0}^{\\pi /4}2e^{t}dt \\\\\n&= 2e^{t} \\mid _{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\\n&= 2(e^{\\pi /4} - 1)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186088945 17592186088946 17592186088947 17592186088948 17592186088949] "immutable_fields" [[17592186088944 :answer-field/correct] [17592186088944 :answer-field/id] [17592186088944 :answer-field/key] [17592186088944 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
